1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Birth date http://denstoredanske.dk/Dansk_Biografisk_Leksikon/Landbrug,_skovbrug_og_gartneri/Forstkandidat/C.H._v._Linstow
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gutshaus-rensow.de/index-5.html The manor house was originally built as a half-timbered building, but the half-timbered façade was largely solidly bricked around 1850-70. The last part of the original timber structure o
2 CONC n the wings of the east side of the manor house was released as part of the facade renovation in 2004. Before 1445 the family Brützekow (Britschow?) Owns the estate. Probably it comes by succession to the family of Bülow. Around t
2 CONC he year 1600 Eler of Lowtzow from Levitzow acquired the estate and village of the family of Bülow.  Other owners were Christof von Lowtzow (1609-1651), Friedrich von Lowtzow (1644-1706), Karl Dietrich von Lowtzow (1686-1769), Frie
2 CONC drich Wilhelm von Lowtzow (1712-1776), August Friedrich von Lowtzow (1749-1820 ), Adolf von Lowtzow (1798-1885), Adolph von Lowtzow (1855-1934), and Werner von Lowtzow (1891-1970).  The family of Lowtzow was expropriated and expel
2 CONC led in 1945, the estate and village were separated. The property went into an LPG. After 1945, the mansion was used as a living space for refugees and displaced persons, later for the employees of the LPG, as well as cafeteria and
2 CONC  social space. In 1990, the farmhouse was separated from agriculture and passed into the possession of the municipality. After that, it was gradually abandoned by its inhabitants. The manor house was sold by the municipality in 20
2 CONC 02. It is currently in the Ahlefeldtschen property.
