1 OCCU Admiralløytnant, Lieutenant
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I Svenska adelskalenderen opplyses at Jens Storm var inspektør for den Svenske flåtes "ekebrygge" i Småland året 1632, det året kong Gustav Adolf falt ved Lutzen. Jens fikk avskjed fra inspektørstillingen i 1643. Å
2 CONC ret etter er han nevnt som løytnant ved Adminiralitetet, en stilling han hadde frem til sin død
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT It is recorded in the Swedish Nobel Calendar (Svenska Adelskalenderen) that Jens Storm served as inspector for the Swedish Navy’s “ekebrygge” in Småland in 1632, the year that King Gustav Adolf was killed at Lutzen.  Jens was rele
2 CONC ased from the inspector position in 1643. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The following year he is noted as being a Lieutenant in the Swedish Navy    (Adminiralitetet), a rank he held until his death in 1655.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Storm’s family originates from the Swedish Lieutenant Jens Storm (mentioned 1632). He was the father of Lieutenant Colonel Balthasar Storm (died 1679), who was ennobled in 1670. 
