1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anders Andersson Appleblom=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Anders Haraldsson Appelbom and Carin Andersdotter, (Hök af Partille) 
2 CONT * County Governor of Härnösand County, War Chamber Councilor,  County Period - 1653 - 1654
2 CONT * Anders Appelbom became king, master of the household in 1645, assessor in the chamber audit in 1650 and finally county governor in Hernösand county (Ångermanland) in 165¾, from which he was dismissed the following year, when thi
2 CONC s county was merged with Gestrikland and Helsingland. He was appointed war chamber councilor in 1661.
2 CONT * He lived on Sörbyholm and seems also to have had literary interests. He is considered to have translated "Harpa af 10 strängar" by doctor Lutkeman, printed in Stockholm in 1678, into Swedish
2 CONT * Appelbom first married on 11 April 1639 to Malin Andersdotter (born 1615), daughter of councilor Anders Andersson and Ingrid Hansdotter Svan in Stockholm . Together they had the children registrar Anders Appelbom and Ingrid Appe
2 CONC lbom (died 1684) who was married to colonel Hieronymus Lindeberg .The son Anders Appelbom was a registrar in the office and is said to have died abroad. As a wife, the latter had a daughter of Daniel Behmer from his first marriage
2 CONC . The latter had a son, Harald Appelbom (1669-1730), court assessor and married to Barbara Magdalena Ehrenhielm whose mother was a Gyldenbring , with whom he had several children who died in infancy, a daughter married to Ehrenhie
2 CONC lm, and the son Harald Appelbom (1711-1783) who was chancellor and married the first time to a Gyldenbring, with whom he had two children who died young. Thus the oldest branch of the family started.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Picture of Anders Andersson Appelbom born 1614 and died 1686 and buried 1687=
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000218267335828&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married ( 1) in 1639-04-11 to '''Malin Andersdotter,''' dotter av rådmannen i Stockholm Anders Andersson och Ingrid Hansdotter Svan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (2) to '''Catharina Gyldenbring,''' dotter av assessorn Erik Bring, adlad Gyldenbring och Catharina Edenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Appelbom_nr_325#TAB_3 Noble Family Appelbom no. 325, by Adelsvapen Genealogies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''TABLE 3 - Anders Appelbom (son of Anders Haraldsson, ennobled Appelbom, tab 1 ).''' Born 1614-01-07. County Governor in Härnösand County. Died 13/10/1686. '''Married 1:o 1639-04-11 to Malin Andersdotter , daughter of the coun
2 CONC cilman in Stockholm Anders Andersson and Ingrid Hansdotter Svan. Married 2nd to Catharina Gyldenbring , daughter of the assessor Erik Bring, ennobled Gyldenbring and Catharina Edenberg .'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Malin Andersdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Anders  Andersson  Appleblom.''' Registrar. (son of Anders Appelbom, table 3 ). Registrar in the Royal Chancellery. Should have then become an officer in Holland and died abroad before 1687. '''Married 1667-06-04 in Stockholm
2 CONC  to Anna Behmer , daughter of court councilor Daniel Behmer and his 1st wife Brita Schulte. born 1669. Deputy attorney general.''' Died 1730. 
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Andersdotter Appleblom,''' died at Lindenäs before 1684-07-25. '''Married to the colonel and deputy governor Hieronymus Lindeberg .'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anders_Appelbom Anders Appelbom, Swedish Governor]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Appelbom , born January 7 , 1614 , died October 13, 1686 , was a Swedish governor in Härnösand County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Appelbom was born in 1614 . He was the son of Anders Haraldsson Appelbom and Carin Andersdotter Hök af Partille . On 29 November 1645, Appelbom became master of household appliances and in 1650 assessor in the chamber audit
2 CONC  . He became governor of Härnösand County on January 29, 1653 , and resigned on March 13, 1653. Appelbom was also a war councilor . He died in 1686 and was buried in Fellingsbro church , where a coat of arms was erected over him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Appelbom owned the farms Söderby and Vässlingbyholm in Fellingsbro parish , Ullevi in ​​Köpings parish and Lunda in Lovö parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Appelbom first married on 11 April 1639 to Malin Andersdotter (born 1615), daughter of councilor Anders Andersson and Ingrid Hansdotter Svan in Stockholm . Together they had the children registrar Anders Appelbom and Ingrid Appelb
2 CONC om (died 1684) who was married to colonel Hieronymus Lindeberg . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Appelbom married the second time to Catharina Gyldenbring (died 1716), daughter of the assessor Erik Gyldenbring and Catharina Edenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In his first marriage, county governor Anders Appelbom had a daughter and a son. The daughter, a new knight, entered into marriage with colonel and vice county governor Hieronymus Lindeberg n :r 379, who was arquebusied in 1677, b
2 CONC ecause he surrendered Landskrona Castle to the Danes, since his wife, who was ill, could not stand the shooting. After the execution of the queen, she received 400 daler in homestead rents as annual maintenance for herself and her
2 CONC  children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://runeberg.org/strokirk/1/0243.html  	Cultural and personal history notes / First part / 239 (1915-1920) MARCH, by Author: Oscar Fredrik Strokirk]
2 CONT
2 CONT II. The second branch of the Appelbom family descends from Anders Appelbom, born 1614 and died 1686 and buried 1687. He rests with his first wife, Malin Anderson, in the Appelbom tomb vault in Fellingsbro church. On either side of
2 CONC  the Appelbom family coat of arms in the chancel are their portraits in full size, carefully renovated in 1896 by the artist Jernberg at a cost of 400 kr. These were originally found on Sörbyholm, but were moved after the reign of
2 CONC  Charles XI, when this property, along with many others, passed out of the family, to the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Appelbom wrote to Sörbyholm and Vesslingsbyholm in Fellingsbro, which included the farms Kjänäs, Harparboda, Åby, Hoboda and to Lunda on Lofön, Ullevi in ​​Köping parish and Risinge in Skunkeby parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had inherited in part, even redeemed all of his father's properties in Fellingsbro except Österhammar with Furunäs and Sköldberga, which went to his brother Samuel and he also increased his estates there through new land acquis
2 CONC itions. He thus became the owner of Spannarboda, Mossboda, a farm in Spånga and Blixter-boda. At Sörbyholm he established a bar iron hammer, which was operated until the beginning of the 19th century. In addition, he purchased or 
2 CONC received in grant a great deal of redemption interest from other farms within the parish. According to the land records, he had, during the lands, partly under the protection of 2 hemman in Nybble, all of Fyrby, Vesslingby, Åby, T
2 CONC åje, Oby, Spångboda, Eskarboda, Östra Boda and Villeboda and 1 hemman in each of Lund and Norra Ekeby.
2 CONT
2 CONT As can be seen from this, the county governor, or as he was usually called, the war councilor Appelbom, was a powerful large landowner and a significant person in Fellingsbro. However, it was not long after his death in 1686 befor
2 CONC e all these properties passed out of the family's possession. Some were sold by the death house to the merchant David Feiff, the rest, including all the redemption interest, were affected by Carl XI's reduction.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders son Anders Appelbom inherited Sörbyholm and Vesslingbyholm in Fellingsbro from his father, but he was only allowed to keep them for four years, because in 1690 they were withdrawn to the crown during the reduction of Charle
2 CONC s VI and did not return further in the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became a war chamberlain, commissar in the Norwegian army in 1658 and registrar in the chancellery. He is said to have finally become an officer in Holland and died abroad. Married to Anna Behmer, born after 1643, daughter of c
2 CONC ourt councillor Daniel Behmer no. 480 and Brita Schütte. Her portrait is kept in the sacristy of Fellingsbro church and has the note on the back "Married to the minister in Holland Harald Anderson son Appelbom", which is obviously
2 CONC  a confusion between her husband and his uncle the minister in The Hague.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Letter to Per Abrahamsson Brahe. From officials. Drätsel.=
